The mathlib_xplane_evaluate() function processes an in-place evaluation of a 32-byte register-equivalent coordinate structure on the Exponent Plane ([X]Plane). It enforces non-commutative geometry mechanics, tracks quality chain degradation classes, handles Rule 4 boundary phase inversions, and computes Rule 9 transfinite collapse limits down to the Euclidean real axis.

Execution runs entirely on the stack or natively inside CPU registers (RAX, RDX, RCX) without dynamic memory allocation (malloc), ensuring predictable bounded latency.

ARGUMENTS
* node: Pointer to a mutable RealIntercept structure representing the working register state.
* options: Bitwise configuration flags of type xplane_opt_t altering runtime logic routing.
